## Why the split is spelled out

CC-BY-3.0 is not one-way compatible with GPLv3 the way CC-BY-4.0 is, so a single
repository-wide license would misstate the terms on one body of work or the
other. Naming the boundary is clearer than leaving it to be inferred from
directory names.
